    ("PARTIAL", 322, "src/engine/registerKinds.json incident · supabase/migrations/0006_workflow_registers_documents.sql register_items_select · supabase/migrations/0012_follow_up_confidentiality.sql · tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T68 T69 · tests/sql/phase2_corrections.sql T143 · tests/ops.test.ts 'a follow-up is as confidential as the record it is linked to' · src/pages/Register360.tsx · supabase/migrations/0013_review_corrections_2.sql follow_ups_follow_record · tests/sql/phase2_corrections_2.sql T152 · tests/ops.test.ts 'a follow-up stays as confidential as its record when the record is reclassified'", "Built: an incident of type 'Extortion / coercion reported' with date, company, reference number, estimated loss, recovered amount, insurance claim reference, report to authorities, reviewer and attached evidence; it can be recorded at a confidentiality level and is then readable only by people cleared for that level; evidence can be neither deleted nor altered (T68, T69); a follow-up linked to the incident takes the confidentiality level of the incident, keeps to it when the level of the incident is changed later, and is read under the same rule (tested on register items, T143 and T152). NUMERO has no function that advises on, routes or disguises such a payment. Not built: separate fields for the amount demanded and the amount paid; legal or compliance status as a field. No test reads a confidential register item itself as a person who is not cleared; the tests cover its follow-ups."),
    ("PARTIAL", 323, "src/engine/registerKinds.json incident · supabase/migrations/0006_workflow_registers_documents.sql register_items_select · tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T68 · src/pages/Register360.tsx", "Built: an incident of type 'Improper payment reported' with date, amount, party, reviewer, recovered amount, notes, attached evidence and a confidentiality level. Documents cannot be deleted (T68); posted entries are corrected by reversal, never erased. NUMI and the engines contain nothing that recommends, calculates or disguises a payment. Not built: suspected or confirmed status, business context, internal investigation reference, legal review and accounting treatment as fields (only notes and a typed state). No test covers this record."),
    ("PARTIAL", 324, "src/engine/registerKinds.json incident · tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T68 T69 · src/pages/Register360.tsx · src/pages/Tasks.tsx", "Built: an incident of type 'Off-book transaction reported'; original evidence is attached and can be neither deleted nor altered (T68, T69); follow-ups record the steps of the investigation and their outcome; correcting entries are ordinary journals under approval, and those tagged to the incident's dimension are listed on its page. Not built: the five stages (record, preserve, investigate, reconcile, correct) as a guided workflow; a direct link from the incident to the correcting journals."),
    ("PARTIAL", 334, "src/engine/registerKinds.json incident · src/pages/Register360.tsx · src/ui/ops.tsx Attachments · supabase/migrations/0006_workflow_registers_documents.sql register_items_select · supabase/migrations/0012_follow_up_confidentiality.sql · tests/sql/phase2_corrections.sql T143 · supabase/migrations/0013_review_corrections_2.sql · tests/sql/phase2_corrections_2.sql T152", "Built: an incident carries one party, attached documents and the posted entries tagged to its dimension, and is readable only by people cleared for its confidentiality level; a follow-up linked to the incident takes that level, keeps to it when the level is changed later, and is read under the same rule (T143, T152). Not built: links from an incident to chosen transactions, payments or several vendors; linkage to a separate whistleblower system."),
    ("PARTIAL", 335, "src/engine/registerKinds.json legal_claim · src/pages/Register360.tsx · tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it'", "Built: a legal case record with case number, forum, legal status, probability as assessed by counsel, potential amount (CONTINGENT and kept out of projected cash, tested), next hearing (watched) and attachments. Not built: legal spend by law firm, court fees, consultants, travel and settlement; total legal spend, outstanding and recoveries. The legal kind creates no cost dimension, so spending cannot be traced to a case."),
