    ("PARTIAL", 415, "tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it' · src/engine/forward.ts cashHorizon · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Built: horizons of today, 7, 14, 30, 60 and 90 days, 6 and 12 months, 3 and 5 years, each with a confidence label and the reason for it (tested). Not built: a Tomorrow horizon. Uncertainty is expressed through the share of firm amounts in the horizon, not through its length, so a long horizon made of contracted items is shown with high confidence."),
    ("TESTED", 416, "tests/forward.test.ts 'an estimate never replaces the contractual date', 'the payroll forecast is labelled FORECAST and says what it leaves out' · tests/numiOps.test.ts 'firm and uncertain amounts are never added into one unlabelled figure' · src/lib/forwardData.ts · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Sources used: open invoices and bills, approved purchase orders, register items (contracts, subscriptions, recurring expenses, sales orders, quotations), loan schedules, deposits, payroll runs, claims, advances, and each customer's past payment delay. Every amount carries its certainty, and estimates are labelled ESTIMATE or FORECAST. Approved budgets and management assumptions are not used as sources."),
    ("PARTIAL", 417, "src/lib/forwardData.ts · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Built: Forward is recalculated from the records each time it is opened, so settled documents drop out and the payroll forecast starts after the last posted run. Not built: a month-by-month statement of actual months followed by forecast months; nothing is stored as a forecast."),
    ("TESTED", 419, "tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it', 'daily balance ends where the horizon ends' · tests/numiOps.test.ts 'a projection is labelled FORECAST and INFERENCE, and starts from ACTUAL cash' · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Opening cash is the ledger balance of bank and cash accounts; collections, contracted inflows, vendor payments, payroll, tax deadlines, loan instalments, rent, capital purchases and other outflows are categories; the closing figure is projected cash for the chosen horizon. It is a projection from recorded items. Payroll is the net pay of the last posted run repeated; statutory and tax remittances are not projected. Tax and capital purchases appear only when a person has recorded them with an amount."),
