    ("PARTIAL", 619, "src/pages/Cockpit.tsx", "Built: panels for cash, profit, revenue, expenditure, receivables, payables, treasury (borrowings and investments together), tax, risk, approvals, anomalies, NUMI and integrity. Not built: panels for payroll, projects, assets, inventory, budget, forecast, audit, autopilot and black vault; debt and investments as separate panels."),
    ("PARTIAL", 666, "tests/forward.test.ts 'every event names its source, its certainty and how it was arrived at', 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it' · tests/numiOps.test.ts 'firm and uncertain amounts are never added into one unlabelled figure' · tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T72 · src/engine/forward.ts", "Built: every future amount carries one of DUE, CONTRACTED, COMMITTED, SCHEDULED, EXPECTED, PROBABLE, POSSIBLE, CONTINGENT or FORECAST; ACTUAL is used only for the cash of today; contingent amounts are kept out of every projection (tested); firm and other amounts are shown as separate figures. Not built: SIMULATION, because no what-if exists. The all-in projection adds firm, expected, possible and forecast amounts into one figure, labelled FORECAST, with the firm-only figure beside it."),
    ("PARTIAL", 668, "src/engine/registerKinds.json quotation · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/pages/Register360.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "Built: a quotation is a register item with customer, amount, currency, probability entered by a person, expected date, products or services and a validity date (watched); it is POSSIBLE, never posts to the ledger and is never counted as firm. The seven stages (draft, sent, negotiating, accepted, rejected, expired, converted) are among the states offered on the screen, which are the ones the database accepts. Not built: conversion of an accepted quotation into an order or invoice (the state 'converted' is chosen by a person and creates nothing); movement from one stage to the next with its date as a pipeline (a change of state is kept in the history of the item only). No test covers quotations to customers."),
    ("TESTED", 671, "tests/forward.test.ts 'a monthly obligation falls due once a month', 'stops at the end date unless it renews automatically', 'every event names its source, its certainty and how it was arrived at' · src/pages/Register360.tsx · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "A contract recorded in the registers with its amount and frequency is CONTRACTED; its payment schedule is listed for twelve months on its own page and for five years in Forward, with any agreed escalation. The contract is entered by a person; nothing is read from the document."),
    ("PARTIAL", 672, "tests/sql/phase2_treasury_purchasing.sql T97 · tests/forward.test.ts 'an approved purchase order is COMMITTED for what has not been billed' · src/pages/PurchaseDetail.tsx · src/pages/Purchasing.tsx", "Built: an approved order is COMMITTED for its unbilled part whether or not a bill has arrived (tested, T97); the order page shows budget, actual to date, this order not yet billed and budget left, by ledger. Not built: a committed figure that includes every open order against the same budget, so the budget left is overstated when other orders are open; the budget context is by ledger for the whole year, not by department or project, and has no test."),
    ("TESTED", 674, "tests/forward.test.ts 'a monthly obligation falls due once a month', 'stops at the end date unless it renews automatically', 'an occurrence already past is kept once, as overdue', 'rent escalation: 10 lakh a month, 5% from April (spec 675)', 'the payroll forecast is labelled FORECAST and says what it leaves out', 'a scheduled occurrence that has already been billed is not counted twice', 'a bill from another party, a cancelled bill or a bill of another period covers nothing' · tests/sql/phase2_treasury_purchasing.sql T85 · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/pages/Register360.tsx · tests/forward.test.ts 'only the bill itself stands for the period: a debit note or a credit note covers nothing'", "Occurrences are calculated from the recorded amount, frequency, start, end, automatic renewal and escalation for rent, lease, software, subscriptions, insurance, maintenance contracts, retainers and utilities; instalments come from the loan schedule; payroll repeats the last posted run and is labelled FORECAST. Nothing is posted or paid by the schedule. In Forward an occurrence is left out when a purchase bill (for money going out) or a sales invoice (for money coming in) from the same party is recorded within half a period of its date — a debit note or a credit note stands for nothing —, so the same obligation is not counted twice, and the screen lists what was left out (tested); this is an inference from party and date, not a link to the bill, and an item without a party is never matched. The next due date does not advance by itself: a person moves it, and an occurrence that has passed and has no such bill stays listed as overdue."),
    ("PARTIAL", 676, "tests/forward.test.ts 'the payroll forecast is labelled FORECAST and says what it leaves out' · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/pages/PeopleCost.tsx", "Built: before salaries are paid, a posted payroll is shown as DUE, and the following months repeat the last posted regular run, labelled FORECAST with what it leaves out (tested). Not built: approved increments, known bonuses, commission, incentives, known adjustments, joiners and leavers; Forward repeats net pay only, so statutory and tax remittances are not projected. A payroll run that is calculated but not posted is not used."),
    ("TESTED", 678, "tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T51 T56 T58 · tests/ops.test.ts 'excess expense becomes a reimbursement due, then paid' · src/pages/Expenses.tsx · src/pages/ClaimEditor.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "A submitted claim is shown as CLAIM PENDING and is no liability; after approval and posting of its entry it is PAYABLE; after the reimbursement entry is posted it is SETTLED. Forward shows a pending claim as POSSIBLE and a payable claim as DUE."),
    ("PARTIAL", 679, "src/engine/registerKinds.json work_order · src/pages/Register360.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "Built: a Work Order register item with contract value, work completed, certified, retention % and retention held, estimated cost to complete with the name of the estimator, next payment date and amount, and the posted entries tagged to the project dimension. Not built: billed and paid as figures of the work order, remaining commitment and forecast final cost (none is calculated). No test covers this kind."),
    ("PARTIAL", 681, "src/engine/registerKinds.json capital_call, capital_infusion, dividend · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "Built: capital calls (with total commitment and called to date), capital infusions and dividends or distributions are register items shown in Forward as EXPECTED, apart from the books. Not built: management fees, fund expenses and portfolio investment commitments as kinds; investor accounting itself."),
    ("TESTED", 682, "tests/sql/phase2_treasury_purchasing.sql T85 T90 · tests/forward.test.ts 'loan position and debt ladder' · tests/ops.test.ts 'loan schedule, disbursement and instalments in order' · src/pages/Loan360.tsx · src/pages/Treasury.tsx", "Each loan shows principal, interest paid and remaining, the instalment, the next payment, the full schedule, maturity, a balloon at the end where the last principal is more than three times the first, and the rate reset date of a floating loan. The schedule is not recalculated at a rate reset; interest on a floating loan is marked indicative."),
    ("PARTIAL", 683, "src/engine/registerKinds.json credit_card · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "Built: a Credit / Corporate Card register item with card holder, last four digits, limit, statement day, payment due day and an expected payment amount and date entered by a person, shown in Forward as EXPECTED. Not built: current unbilled amount, statement amount, expected recurring charges and available limit; there is no card feed or statement import."),
    ("TESTED", 684, "tests/forward.test.ts 'stops at the end date unless it renews automatically', 'rent escalation: 10 lakh a month, 5% from April (spec 675)' · tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T72 · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/pages/Register360.tsx", "A subscription records cost and frequency (annualised on Registers), renewal date, automatic renewal, cancel-by date, an agreed price increase (percentage and date) and end date. The schedule stops at the end date unless the item renews automatically, and the increase applies from its date (tested on the schedule engine). A price increase is what a person records; NUMERO does not detect one."),
    ("PARTIAL", 685, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions' · src/engine/registerKinds.json insurance, insurance_claim · src/pages/Register360.tsx", "Built: an insurance policy with premium and frequency, policy expiry (watched), renewal date, cover type, sum insured and what is insured; expiry and renewal raise warnings (tested). Not built: an expected renewal premium separate from the current premium (only an agreed escalation percentage); claims listed against the policy (an insurance claim item carries the policy number as text)."),
    ("PARTIAL", 686, "src/engine/registerKinds.json warranty · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/pages/Register360.tsx", "Built: a Warranty Given register item with product, customer, period (start and end date), known claims and an estimated obligation entered by a person, held as CONTINGENT. Not built: historical claims; any calculation of the estimated obligation."),
    ("TESTED", 687, "tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it' · src/engine/registerKinds.json legal_claim · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/pages/Register360.tsx", "A legal case records the claim, potential amount, legal status, probability class as assessed by counsel with the name of the assessor, expected timing and the approved accounting treatment. The amount is CONTINGENT and stays outside projected cash (the test uses the legal claim in the sample data). NUMERO does not estimate probability or liability: those fields are filled by a person."),
    ("TESTED", 688, "tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it' · tests/numiOps.test.ts 'contingent exposure is shown beside the projection, not inside it' · src/engine/registerKinds.json contingent_liability · src/pages/Registers.tsx", "Lawsuits, guarantees, disputed taxes, warranty claims and contract disputes are recorded as contingent register items. A register item never posts to the ledger, so nothing becomes a liability unless a person records an entry. Contingent amounts are reported beside the projection (tested)."),
    ("PARTIAL", 690, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions', 'a guarantee given is contingent: beside the projection, never inside it' · src/engine/registerKinds.json bank_guarantee, letter_of_credit · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/pages/Registers.tsx", "Built: warnings for guarantee expiry and claim expiry (tested) and for the settlement date and expiry of a letter of credit; the amount of a letter of credit is a COMMITTED outflow in Forward; a guarantee given is shown in Forward as a CONTINGENT amount dated at its expiry, beside the projection and never inside it, as the cash that would be needed if it were called (tested); Registers totals contingent exposure. Not built: margin and fees in the forward view (they are recorded on the item only)."),
    ("PARTIAL", 691, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions' · src/engine/registerKinds.json compliance · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/pages/Cockpit.tsx", "Built: tax and compliance deadlines for GST, TDS, income tax and payroll statutory dues, with an amount entered by a person and a note of how it was estimated, shown in Forward as EXPECTED; the cockpit shows net tax payable from the ledger. Not built: any tax estimate calculated by NUMERO; TCS and customs as choices; the label ESTIMATED TAX."),
    ("PARTIAL", 692, "src/engine/registerKinds.json asset_purchase · src/pages/Purchasing.tsx · src/pages/Assets.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "Built: a Planned Asset Purchase register item appears in Forward as capital expenditure; separately, requisition, order and receipt have their own statuses in Purchasing, and an asset is recorded in the asset register. Not built: one pipeline that carries a purchase from requested to approved, ordered, delivered, capitalised and paid; a link between the planned purchase, the order and the asset."),
    ("PARTIAL", 693, "tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T40 T41 · src/engine/registerKinds.json asset_sale · src/pages/Asset360.tsx", "Built: a Planned Asset Sale register item with expected sale value and buyer; the sale itself is a proposed disposal entry with proceeds, receipt into a bank or cash ledger and gain or loss (T40, T41). Not built: offer and agreement as tracked stages; a link between the planned sale, the asset and its disposal."),
    ("PARTIAL", 694, "tests/forward.test.ts 'depreciation forecast follows the recorded method' · src/engine/ops.ts depreciationForecast · src/pages/Assets.tsx · src/pages/Asset360.tsx", "Built: depreciation for the next twelve months for each existing asset and in total, by the recorded method, labelled as a forecast (tested). Not built: depreciation on approved planned capital expenditure."),
    ("PARTIAL", 696, "src/engine/registerKinds.json dividend · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "Built: a Dividend / Distribution register item with amount, date, declaration date and approval reference, shown in Forward as EXPECTED. Not built: the stages proposed, board approved, declared, payable and paid as a tracked pipeline — the state is chosen from the list the database accepts, which has proposed, approved, due and paid but neither declared nor payable; any posting of the dividend."),
    ("PARTIAL", 697, "src/engine/registerKinds.json csr_donation · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/pages/Register360.tsx", "Built: a CSR / Donation Commitment register item with beneficiary (party), purpose, approval reference, committed amount and date, and supporting documents. Not built: proposal and approval as a workflow; a link to the payment; compliance classification."),
    ("PARTIAL", 698, "src/engine/registerKinds.json customer_refund · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "Built: a Customer Refund Due register item with reason, original invoice or receipt reference, amount and date, shown in Forward as a COMMITTED outflow. Not built: the stages requested, reviewed, approved, payable, paid and rejected as a tracked pipeline with approval; a link to the refund payment or credit note."),
    ("PARTIAL", 699, "src/pages/Owed.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts earlyWarnings · src/engine/registerKinds.json bad_debt", "Built: receivables as current and overdue by age; a warning when one customer holds 30% or more of receivables; a Doubtful / Bad Debt register item with the invoices concerned, the provision recorded and the assessment by finance. Nothing writes off a balance on its own. Not built: classification of receivables as disputed, collection risk, provisioned or written off; configuration of the policy."),
    ("TESTED", 702, "tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it', 'daily balance ends where the horizon ends' · src/engine/forward.ts cashHorizon · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "The cash horizon has exactly the ten horizons listed: today, 7, 14, 30, 60 and 90 days, 6 and 12 months, 3 and 5 years (the test asserts the list). It projects from recorded documents and registers; the only estimate is the customer's usual payment delay, used when the person chooses it and labelled ESTIMATE."),
    ("TESTED", 704, "tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it' · src/engine/forward.ts cashHorizon · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/numi/ops.ts", "Each horizon is marked HIGH, MEDIUM or LOW with a sentence that says why: the share of amounts that are due, contracted, committed or scheduled, and the share of inflows already overdue. It is a rule on recorded amounts, not a statistical band."),
    ("PARTIAL", 706, "src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents", "Built: a payment priority view of outflows for the next 60 days with due date, what, party, amount, certainty and days overdue, and the statement that a person decides what to pay. Not built: penalty, contract terms and criticality classification; available cash beside the list (cash today is shown elsewhere on the same screen)."),
    ("PARTIAL", 707, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions', 'a cash shortfall names its causes and assumptions', 'notices rise at 60, 30 and 7 days (spec 712)', 'dependence on one vendor is stated beside dependence on one customer' · src/engine/forward.ts earlyWarnings · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/numi/ops.ts", "Built: warnings for projected cash below a threshold, payroll cover, loan instalments within 30 days, renewals, cancel-by dates, expiries and deadlines within 90 days (the level rises at 60, 30 and 7 days), expiring documents, maturing deposits, advances past their settlement date, concentration of receivables with one customer and of payables with one vendor, and promises that have passed; each states facts and assumptions (tested; the warning on receivables has no test of its own). Not built: continuous monitoring. Warnings are calculated when Forward is opened or NUMI is asked; they are not stored, not shown on Home or in the menu, and nothing is sent. The cash threshold is kept in the browser only."),
    ("TESTED", 710, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions', 'loan position and debt ladder' · tests/numiOps.test.ts 'debt: principal outstanding agrees with the loan schedule' · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/pages/Loan360.tsx · src/pages/Treasury.tsx", "Forward warns of loan instalments that fall due within 30 days, with each amount and date, and lists every instalment for five years with its principal and interest. A balloon payment is identified on the page of the loan, not in the warning. Shown inside the application only."),
    ("TESTED", 711, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions' · src/engine/forward.ts earlyWarnings · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/engine/registerKinds.json compliance", "A tax or compliance deadline raises a warning with the requirement, the due date, the amount where one is recorded and the owner as the responsible person. The amount is what a person entered; the cash required is that same amount. The deadlines in the sample data carry no amount. For a recurring deadline a person moves the next due date."),
    ("PARTIAL", 712, "tests/forward.test.ts 'notices rise at 60, 30 and 7 days (spec 712)', 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions' · src/engine/forward.ts noticeLevel, earlyWarnings · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Built: a warning is shown from 90 days before a renewal, cancel-by, end or watched date, for information; its level rises at 60 days (review), at 30 days (priority) and at 7 days (critical), and it stays critical once the date has passed (tested). Not built: alerts as messages — the warning is one line in Forward whose level changes, seen by a person who opens Forward or asks NUMI, and nothing is stored or sent at the four points; configuration of the notice periods."),
    ("IMPLEMENTED", 713, "src/engine/forward.ts earlyWarnings · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/engine/registerKinds.json subscription", "Before a renewal or a cancel-by date Forward shows the cost and frequency of the subscription, its owner (or that none is recorded), the cancel-by date and whether it renews automatically. Usage is not shown: no integration provides it. The test of early warnings does not assert a subscription renewal specifically."),
    ("TESTED", 714, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions' · src/engine/registerKinds.json insurance, vehicle · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Insurance policies carry a cover type (vehicle, office, equipment, marine, liability, health, life, fire, other) and an expiry date that is watched; vehicles carry their own insurance expiry. A warning is shown from 90 days before the date and after it has passed (the test asserts that insurance expiry warnings are raised). Shown inside the application only."),
    ("PARTIAL", 715, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions' · src/engine/forward.ts earlyWarnings · src/engine/registerKinds.json bank_guarantee · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Built: a warning for the expiry and the claim expiry of a guarantee from 90 days before, naming the recorded owner (tested). Not built: notifying the responsible user. The warning is visible only to a person who opens Forward or asks NUMI; nothing is sent."),
    ("PARTIAL", 718, "tests/forward.test.ts 'budget exhaustion is a statement with assumptions, not a verdict' · src/engine/forward.ts budgetExhaustion", "Built: the calculation and its wording ('may be exhausted in approximately X months', with run rate, commitments and assumptions), tested. Not built: no screen and no NUMI answer calls it, and no department budget feeds it, so nobody can see this forecast."),
    ("TESTED", 722, "tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it', 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions' · src/engine/forward.ts cashHorizon · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Forward opens with four panels for today and the next 7, 30 and 90 days, each with expected inflows and outflows, the firm part of each, net position, projected cash and the number of warnings dated inside the window. Figures are numbers with labels, not colour alone. The figures come from the tested horizon engine; the count of warnings per panel is screen logic without a test."),
    ("PARTIAL", 723, "tests/numiOps.test.ts 'a projection is labelled FORECAST and INFERENCE, and starts from ACTUAL cash', 'renewals and expiries come from recorded dates', 'commitments are labelled COMMITTED and agree with the engine', 'gives totals and never names a person', 'the wording of the specification's own example questions' · src/numi/ops.ts · src/numi/engine.ts", "Built: NUMI answers, from the records and with labels, how much cash there would be in a number of days with inflows and outflows split into firm and other, which renewals and expiries are close (including 'What insurance expires?'), what is committed on purchase orders, what the last payroll cost, and what debt falls due. Questions worded with 'renew', 'next month' or 'next quarter' are recognised as forward questions (tested: 'Which contracts renew next month?', 'How much cash will we likely need next month?'). The eleven example questions were put to NUMI on the sample data on 2026-09-27. Not built: what-if questions (a customer paying 60 days late) and a tax estimate, which receive the reply that they cannot be answered from the books; uncommitted cash as a figure ('How much cash is truly uncommitted?' is answered with what is committed on purchase orders); projects that may exceed budget (answered with budget lines by ledger and company); payroll still to come (the payroll answer gives the last posted month); renewals by kind or by period — a question about contracts, subscriptions or insurance, this month or next quarter, receives every renewal and expiry inside the notice period of 90 days; 'next month' is taken as the next 61 days."),
    ("PARTIAL", 784, "src/engine/registerKinds.json incident, recovery, insurance_claim · src/pages/Register360.tsx", "Built: an incident records estimated loss and one recovered amount; insurance claims and recovery cases are separate register items with amount claimed, approved by the insurer, received and recovered to date. Not built: gross loss, insurance recovery, legal recovery and net loss as figures of one case; net loss is not calculated; the separate items are not linked to the incident."),
    ("PARTIAL", 785, "src/engine/registerKinds.json recovery · src/pages/Registers.tsx · tests/sql/phase2_treasury_purchasing.sql T109 · tests/sql/phase2_payroll.sql T121", "Built: a Recovery Case register item with the party, what is being recovered, recovered to date and method (follow-up, negotiation, legal, insurance, payroll recovery, other); recovery of an advance through payroll is posted and tested (T109, T121). Not built: the kind of recovery (employee, vendor, bank, insurance, legal settlement, asset) as a field; posting of a recovery from the recovery case."),
    ("PARTIAL", 796, "src/engine/registerKinds.json incident · src/pages/Register360.tsx · supabase/migrations/0006_workflow_registers_documents.sql register_items_select", "Built: an incident of type 'Whistleblower report' with one party, attached documents and a confidentiality level that limits who can read it. Not built: links to a transaction, an employee or a case; protection of the identity of the reporter apart from the record (the 'reported by' field is visible to everyone who can read the incident); linkage to a separate whistleblower system."),
    ("PARTIAL", 797, "supabase/migrations/0004_reporting_sentinel_numi.sql run_sentinel · supabase/migrations/0007_assets_purchasing.sql · tests/sql/phase2_treasury_purchasing.sql T100 T102 · src/pages/Sentinel.tsx", "Built: factual flags for a large payment to a newly created party, a bill for more than was received or ordered (T100, T102), large round-number manual journals, amounts just below an approval threshold, entries at unusual times and possible duplicates. The wording states the rule and never alleges bribery. Not built: flags for unusual cash payments, consultant payments without explanation, payment without a deliverable where no purchase order exists, vague invoices, commission outside the contracted rule and payments to unknown intermediaries."),
    ("PARTIAL", 798, "src/engine/registerKinds.json incident · src/pages/Register360.tsx · src/ui/ops.tsx Attachments", "Built: a protected incident (confidentiality level) of type 'Extortion / coercion reported' with attached documents, insurance claim reference, report to authorities and reviewer. NUMERO has no function that facilitates or disguises a payment. Not built: links to payments and communications; insurance and legal review as linked records (text fields only)."),
    ("PARTIAL", 810, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions', 'an estimate never replaces the contractual date' · src/ui/records.tsx · numero_private.save_promise · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Built: a promise to pay is recorded against the invoice and shown in Forward as PROMISED; when its date passes, a warning asks a person to record whether it was kept (tested); once it is recorded as not kept, the receivable falls back to its due date or the usual delay of the customer; the projection is recalculated each time Forward is opened. Not built: the change to a missed promise on its own; a collection follow-up created from it (a follow-up cannot be linked to an invoice from the invoice screen)."),
    ("PARTIAL", 812, "tests/forward.test.ts 'every event names its source, its certainty and how it was arrived at' · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts", "Built: today, 7, 30 and 90 days and 12 months as horizons, with every future event shown with its certainty; items already past their date are marked overdue. Not built: the past on the same timeline (past figures are in the ledger and the reports)."),
    ("PARTIAL", 813, "tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it' · src/pages/Forward.tsx · src/engine/forward.ts cashHorizon", "Built: on Forward, cash today, firm inflows, other inflows, firm outflows, other outflows, commitments, contingent amounts and early warnings, for a chosen horizon. Not built: a simple owner screen under the nine headings; money at risk as a figure."),
    ("PARTIAL", 819, "tests/numiOps.test.ts 'a projection is labelled FORECAST and INFERENCE, and starts from ACTUAL cash' · src/numi/ops.ts · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Built: for the next 30 days, NUMI and Forward give inflows and outflows split into firm and other, projected cash, the largest outflows and up to three warnings of priority or critical level; Forward gives the amounts by category (collections, vendor payments, payroll, taxes, loan repayments, subscriptions). Not built: a brief in the stated form; Sentinel review items in it; renewals as one amount."),
    ("IMPLEMENTED", 820, "tests/sql/phase2_treasury_purchasing.sql T97 · tests/forward.test.ts 'contingent amounts are reported beside the projection, never inside it', 'an estimate never replaces the contractual date' · tests/numiOps.test.ts 'a projection is labelled FORECAST and INFERENCE, and starts from ACTUAL cash' · src/ui/records.tsx · numero_private.save_register_item", "Tested: a purchase order is no expense (T97), a contingent liability stays outside the projection, a forecast is labelled and starts from actual cash, an estimate never replaces the contractual date. Shown by the code, not by a test: a quotation, a signed contract and a guarantee are register items, and saving one creates no journal; a promise to pay changes nothing in the books and is shown as PROMISED. Four of the eight distinctions have no test of their own, so the status is IMPLEMENTED, not TESTED."),
    ("PARTIAL", 1197, "tests/forward.test.ts 'people cost: salary is not the whole cost, and shared costs are not invented' · src/engine/ops.ts peopleCost · src/pages/PeopleCost.tsx", "Built: People cost shows salary, variable pay, employer cost and direct costs per person and in total, and the total is the sum of the four (tested); the page states that these figures are not a measure of performance. Not built: the complete cost. Shared costs are not allocated, equipment held as assets is not counted, and direct costs are read from at most 20,000 ledger entries of the period, page by page (the page warns when the period holds more)."),
    ("PARTIAL", 1212, "tests/forward.test.ts 'people cost: salary is not the whole cost, and shared costs are not invented' · src/engine/ops.ts peopleCost · src/pages/PeopleCost.tsx", "Built: salary, variable pay and employer contributions from posted payroll, and other direct cost where an expense entry names the person, shown by ledger (travel, software and so on appear only if recorded that way). The page states that shared costs are not allocated because no method has been approved. Not built: benefits, equipment, software, travel and vehicle as headings of their own; allocated office cost; an allocation method to show."),
    ("PARTIAL", 1213, "src/engine/ops.ts peopleCost · src/pages/PeopleCost.tsx", "Built: totals of salary, variable pay, employer cost and direct costs for the companies selected; selecting one company gives the figures of that company. Not built: a table by company; bonus and commission as separate figures; benefits, travel and equipment as headings; allocated costs."),
    ("TESTED", 1214, "tests/forward.test.ts 'people cost follows the department recorded on the payroll line, not the person's present department' · tests/sql/phase2_payroll.sql T114 · tests/ops.test.ts 'the payroll journal is confidential, by department, and names no one' · src/engine/ops.ts peopleCost · src/pages/PeopleCost.tsx", "People cost shows headcount, salary and total cost by department, as a chart and a table. Salary, variable pay and employer cost are counted in the department recorded on the payroll line, so a later transfer does not move earlier months (tested), and the payroll journal is charged by department in the same way (T114). Direct costs recorded against a person carry no department of their own in this calculation and follow the department the person belongs to today. The departments are those the company defines; none of the seven named in the requirement is supplied. The chart and the table on the screen draw on the tested calculation and have no test of their own."),
    ("IMPLEMENTED", 1216, "src/pages/PeopleCost.tsx · src/lib/data.ts", "People cost shows people cost as a percentage of revenue and revenue per employee for the selected period, each with its formula and inputs, and states that the ratios describe the business, not any person. No test covers these two figures. The people cost used includes direct costs, which are read from at most 20,000 ledger entries of the period, page by page; the page warns when the period holds more."),
