    ("PARTIAL", 1480, "tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T48 T52 T62 T75 T76 T77 · tests/ops.test.ts 'reversal keeps documents truthful' · src/engine/registerKinds.json · numero_private.create_payroll_run", "Built: advances with partial settlement and return (T52), reversal of receipts and invoices with the documents kept truthful (T75 to T77), a missing receipt flagged as EVIDENCE MISSING (T48), cash count differences (T62), warnings for contract renewal, pay up to the exit date of a leaving employee, and from phase 1 partial payment and the alert on a change of bank details. Not built: refund, security deposit and retention as workflows (they are register items that post nothing); final settlement of a leaving employee as a guided process; unidentified cash and unreconciled differences beyond the suspense and bank reconciliation screens of phase 1."),
    ("TESTED", 1487, "tests/forward.test.ts 'every event names its source, its certainty and how it was arrived at' · tests/numiOps.test.ts 'a projection is labelled FORECAST and INFERENCE, and starts from ACTUAL cash' · src/engine/forward.ts · src/pages/Forward.tsx", "Forward is a screen and an engine of its own. Commitments (purchase orders), obligations, contracts, expected income, expected expenses, tax deadlines, renewals and project work orders (registers), payroll, debt (loan schedule) and collections (open invoices and promises) are each a source of forward events with a certainty; the test asserts that all nine sources produce events."),
    ("PARTIAL", 1492, "tests/forward.test.ts 'people cost: salary is not the whole cost, and shared costs are not invented' · src/engine/ops.ts peopleCost, workforceOutside · src/pages/PeopleCost.tsx", "Built: salary, variable pay, employer cost, direct costs recorded against the person (travel and the like, by ledger), spending on the contract workforce and a total workforce cost. Not built: benefits, equipment, software and vehicle as headings of their own; allocated office cost. Direct costs and contract workforce figures are read from at most 20,000 ledger entries of the period, page by page; the page warns when the period holds more."),
    ("IMPLEMENTED", 1493, "tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T73 · tests/sql/phase2_payroll.sql T127 T128 · src/pages/Registers.tsx · src/engine/templates.ts · src/engine/registerKinds.json", "No engine or screen names a company or an industry: companies are created from templates, register kinds and their fields are data that a group administrator can add or change (T73), and custom fields are defined per record type (T127, T128). Company names appear only in the sample data. Adding a register kind was not exercised against the live system."),
    ("TESTED", 1567, "tests/sql/phase2_flow.sql T51 T52 T53 T54 · tests/ops.test.ts 'partial settlement leaves a balance that is RETURN DUE, and the return settles it' · src/pages/Advance360.tsx · src/pages/ClaimEditor.tsx", "The example is the test: an advance of 1,00,000, approved expenses of 78,000, and the balance of 22,000 becomes RETURN DUE when the entry of the claim is posted (T52); a return cannot exceed it (T53) and the return settles the advance (T54). The balance turns into RETURN DUE on its own only when the claim is marked as the final settlement of the advance."),
