    ("PARTIAL", 1706, "tests/forward.test.ts 'early warnings state facts, rules and assumptions' · numero_private.save_advance · src/pages/Advance360.tsx · src/pages/Expenses.tsx · src/pages/Cash.tsx", "Built: every advance has a recipient as custodian and a purpose, both required; the expected settlement date is recorded and an advance past it raises a warning (tested); a cash box has a custodian. Not built: the expected settlement date as a required field. Where it is missing, 30 days from release is used for the warning, and the warning says so."),
    ("IMPLEMENTED", 1731, "src/engine/forward.ts buildEvents · src/pages/Forward.tsx · tests/forward.test.ts 'every event names its source, its certainty and how it was arrived at'", "An advance that is approved and not yet released, or released in part, appears in Forward as a COMMITTED outflow for the unreleased amount, with the basis 'Advance approved, money not yet released'. An approved claim awaiting reimbursement and a posted payroll awaiting payment appear as DUE. The test asserts that advances produce forward events; it does not assert the unreleased case specifically."),
    ("PARTIAL", 1833, "tests/sql/phase2_payroll.sql T125 · tests/forward.test.ts 'rent escalation: 10 lakh a month, 5% from April (spec 675)' · numero_private.create_payroll_run · src/pages/Payroll.tsx", "Built: a salary revision carries an effective date and a payroll run uses the approved salary in force for its month, so a revision can be approved ahead of its date (T125 tests that the earlier record remains); an agreed escalation on a register item starts on its date (tested). Not built: a future effective date on configuration in general: register kinds, expense policy, approval rules and custom fields take effect when saved."),
